    {
      "name": "ImtTree",
      "docs": [
        "Incremental Merkle Tree state for inserted deposit commitments.",
        "",
        "Nested inside `RootRegistry`, so this type must be Pod: fixed-size, no",
        "padding holes, so the account bytes can be the struct. `repr(C)` plus",
        "`Pod` / `Zeroable` is that overlay. `#[idl(bytemuck)]` marks it as bytemuck",
        "in the IDL too; without it the IDL lists it as borsh and `declare_program!`",
        "clients generate a non-Pod `ImtTree`, which breaks the bytemuck `RootRegistry`.",
        "",
        "# Fields",
        "",
        "- `root` - current root of the tree (root level == MERKLE_TREE_DEPTH, leaf level == 0)",
        "",
        "- `frontiers` - also called filledSubtrees. It stores exactly one hash per level — the hash of the",
        "  most recently updated left subtree at that level.",
        "  One value per level (no need to store it for root level)",
        "",
        "- `zero_values` - Z_k for each level k (precomputed). Contains MERKLE_TREE_DEPTH values (we do not need it on root level)",
        "",
        "- `next_leaf_idx` - Index of the next leaf to be inserted (0.. 2^MERKLE_TREE_DEPTH)",
        "  First (leaf) level depth == 0 and amount of leafs at this level is 2^MERKLE_TREE_DEPTH",
        "",
        "@dev Note:",
        "frontiers and zero_values store 32-byte scalar field elements in little endian format.",
        "Normally each would be its own `[u8; 32]`, giving a declaration like:",
        "  frontiers: [[u8; 32]; MERKLE_TREE_DEPTH] // TODO: is this the issue also in AnchorV2  or only in Quasar?",
        "The levels are flattened and indexed by hand through [`get_array_element`] / [`set_array_element`]:",
        "  frontiers: [u8; 32 * MERKLE_TREE_DEPTH] // MERKLE_TREE_DEPTH levels of 32 bytes each"
      ],
      "serialization": "bytemuck",
      "repr": {
        "kind": "c"
      },
      "type": {
        "kind": "struct",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "root",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                32
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "frontiers",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                640
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "zero_values",
            "type": {
              "array": [
                "u8",
                640
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "next_leaf_idx",
            "type": {
              "defined": {
                "name": "PodU32"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
